  "description": "PIVZIF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C144 H153 Eu9 O58,2(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu7 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu8 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu9 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.630-5.161 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.23-173.17°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu9(L1)16(μ3-OH)8(μ4-O)(μ4-OH)]·2H2O·2CH3OH (anal. Eu9C146H165O62). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
